WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.460
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:14.598
The AI tab, part three: the jobs that make up the world as you play,

5
00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:17.922
encounters, items, new abilities and places.

6
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:21.997
Open the AI tab, then Encounter Elements.

7
00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:27.390
These are lists of ideas the AI draws on when it makes up an encounter on the road,

8
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.690
grouped by category.

9
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.769
Voyage ships twenty one of them.

10
00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:35.211
I added one for us, Circus Road: broken-down wagons,

11
00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:39.418
rival circus posters, toll bridges with greedy keepers.

12
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:46.952
Encounters is the job that turns those ideas into encounters while you travel through the wild.

13
00:00:46.952 --> 00:00:53.070
Ours says what turns up by day and by night, and that about half shouldn't need a fight at all.

14
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:58.533
Item Generation and Usage covers how items are found, bought and used.

15
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:04.923
The most important rule here: nothing goes in the inventory until the player actually takes it or pays for it,

16
00:01:04.923 --> 00:01:08.350
or the AI hands things over the moment you look at a stall.

17
00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.255
Ours has that, our prices, and what bandits carry.

18
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:16.739
Learned Abilities makes up new moves characters learn in play.

19
00:01:16.739 --> 00:01:21.664
Ability tier tells it to sort each one into the tiers from combat settings.

20
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.623
Our custom says what can be learned, circus tricks,

21
00:01:25.623 --> 00:01:29.008
road skills and cons, and what can't: real magic.

22
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.675
Location Details writes up places the AI fills in.

23
00:01:33.675 --> 00:01:38.128
Ours says what a trade-road town has, and to give one thing you see,

24
00:01:38.128 --> 00:01:41.534
one you hear, and how the town feels about the show.

25
00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:48.643
And Region Details writes new regions: ours are farm country on the old trade roads,

26
00:01:48.643 --> 00:01:52.314
with towns named plainly after what they're known for.

27
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.621
One tip from Voyage's docs.

28
00:01:55.621 --> 00:02:00.316
What a single item does goes in that item's description, not here.

29
00:02:00.316 --> 00:02:05.438
This box is for general rules, and crafting rules belong in Action Info.

30
00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.469
That's the AI tab done.

31
00:02:08.469 --> 00:02:11.813
Our instructions are linked in the description.

32
00:02:11.813 --> 00:02:15.796
Next time, audio: voices and the rest of the music page.

33
00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:20.181
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

